<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44202" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signācŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		signo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a mark</i>, <i>a sign</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporis,</span>”
				i.e. <i>circumcision</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontis inscripta oleo,</span>”
				i.e. <i>the sign of the cross</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 360</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>a seal</i>, <i>signet</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. Flor. 2, p. 346</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 16, 3, 1, § 36</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Novat. Th. 2</span></i>, tit. 16, c. 1,
			§ 5. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
